<main>
<header>
<h1>Reconstruct which GitHub Action commit actually ran—even after a mutable tag was restored.</h1>
<p class="lede">CIRewind is an experimental, evidence-first command-line tool that rebuilds historical GitHub Actions execution from retained evidence. This deterministic synthetic sample is not a real incident.</p>
</header>

<div class="hero">
<section id="temporal-evidence-path">
<h2>Temporal evidence path</h2>
<div class="visual" role="region" aria-label="Temporal evidence path, scrollable visual" tabindex="0">
<img src="./graph.svg" alt="Temporal evidence path for the synthetic case: one lane per finding showing exact observations as solid lines, inferences as dashed lines, temporal correlation as dotted lines, contradictions as heavy lines, and evidence gaps as interrupted lines, each labeled with its relationship and evidence references." width="{{.SVGWidth}}" height="{{.SVGHeight}}">
</div>
<p><a href="./graph.svg">Open the standalone SVG</a>. The visual is a projection of the case database; it is not an attack graph and it adds no evidence.</p>
</section>
<div>
<section id="results">
