<section id="demonstrates">
<h2>What the A-to-B-to-A case demonstrates</h2>
<ul>
<li>A mutable <code>v1</code> tag that resolved to commit B: the exact B lifecycle start supports <code>CONFIRMED_EXECUTED</code>.</li>
<li>B downloaded without execution: preparation completed but no step began, so the state stays <code>CONFIRMED_DOWNLOADED</code>.</li>
<li>Rerun attempts remain separate by <code>run_id + run_attempt + job_id</code>; the restored-A attempt is a comparison lane, not an affected run.</li>
<li>Restoring the tag to A does not rewrite the historical B evidence.</li>
<li>Missing logs stay <code>UNKNOWN_EVIDENCE_GAP</code>; they never become a clean result.</li>
<li>Context relationships are reported as capability or relationship, never as proven access: {{.WriteTokenJobs}} affected job with a write-capable <code>GITHUB_TOKEN</code> permission, {{.NamedSecretFlows}} named-secret flow to an affected step, {{.OIDCJobs}} affected job with OIDC minting capability, {{.SelfHostedJobs}} affected job on a self-hosted runner, and {{.DeploymentsAfter}} deployment observed after an affected step with causation not established.</li>
</ul>
</section>

