<section id="install">
<h2>Installation lanes</h2>
<p>The fast evaluation lane above relies on Homebrew for integrity. With the supported Go toolchain, the module ecosystem provides the same evaluation build:</p>
<pre><code>go install github.com/torjan0/cirewind/cmd/cirewind@v{{.Version}}
cirewind demo --out cirewind-demo
cirewind verify cirewind-demo</code></pre>
<p>The high-assurance lane downloads the reproducible release archives from the <a href="{{.ReleaseURL}}" rel="noreferrer">{{.Version}} release page</a>, verifies build-provenance attestations, <code>SHA256SUMS</code>, and per-target SPDX documents before extraction, and remains the recommended path for forensic use. Release binaries report their exact version, source revision, and build time; an evaluation build reports the module version and an unknown commit rather than inventing one.</p>
</section>

<section id="limits">
<h2>Experimental qualification and limitations</h2>
<p>CIRewind {{.Version}} is experimental. Its controlled qualification covers GitHub.com explicit-repository collection for direct, downloaded-only, composite, reusable, matrix, and rerun scenarios. Organization completeness at GitHub's result ceiling, every credential type, every runner grammar, and full downstream resource inventories remain limitations. This sample deliberately reports partial coverage: an evidence gap is shown as a gap.</p>
<p>GitHub evidence alone cannot prove that a secret value was read, that a cloud role was used, that a runner kept state, or that a later deployment was intended by anyone. CIRewind reports capabilities, relationships, and temporal order, and it separates each from causation.</p>
</section>

<section id="privacy">
<h2>Privacy and provenance</h2>
<ul>
<li>Every identity on this site is synthetic. No real repository, run, secret, or person appears.</li>
<li>The project adds no analytics, telemetry, cookies, storage, forms, or uploads to this site, and it never receives a visitor's case. GitHub logs visitor IP addresses for Pages sites for security purposes.</li>
<li>Generated from source revision <code>{{.SourceCommit}}</code> with <code>{{.GoVersion}}</code>, demo bundle <code>{{.DemoBundleID}}</code>, synthetic pack version <code>{{.FixtureVersion}}</code>.</li>
<li>Case manifest SHA-256 <code>{{.CaseManifestSHA256}}</code>; archive SHA-256 <code>{{.ArchiveSHA256}}</code>; the site manifest covers every versioned file. Manifest checks support integrity, not authenticity or legal custody.</li>
<li>Regenerate locally with <code>make sample-site SITE_VERSION={{.Version}} SITE_OUT=DIR</code> from the same source revision; the output is byte-identical.</li>
<li>Source: <a href="{{.ProjectURL}}" rel="noreferrer">{{.ProjectURL}}</a>. Independent reproductions of the public laboratory are indexed at <a href="{{.LabIndexURL}}" rel="noreferrer">{{.LabIndexURL}}</a>; an empty index makes no reproduction claim.</li>
</ul>
</section>
